  "releaseNotes": "GetDataModelParameters, and so the query methods, Fill and ReduceToUnique, read a JSON integer from 2^53 (9007199254740992) on, of either sign, as a long, with every digit, up to the largest long. It was a double, which can't tell such neighbouring integers apart: 9007199254740993 became 9007199254740992, and a query by either id found both rows. Every other JSON number is still a double, so the SQL that reads it computes and compares as before. A caller that casts such a value to double must convert it instead (Convert.ToDouble). The Microsoft Access ODBC driver rejects a long parameter (Optional feature not implemented), so there such a number now fails where it was rounded.",
